scription":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-09-07T20:57:57Z","updated_at":"2026-09-10T12:49:10Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in:\n- v4.7.stable.mono.official [5b4e0cb0f]\n- v4.7.2.stable.official [ed1daf0bf]\n\n### System information\n\nmacOS Tahoe 26.6\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen `use_texture_padding` is on for a `TileSetAtlasSource` and the `TileMapLayer` is freed, the RID will be double-freed and lead to errors like this:\n\n```\nE 0:00:01:961   _free_internal: Attempted to free invalid ID: 7206955122706\n  <C++ Source>  servers/rendering/rendering_device.cpp:7744 @ _free_internal()\n```\n\nFull disclosure: I hit this bug in my game, asked AI to fix it, and it found this seemingly novel cause in Godot itself. AI created the MRP, but I did not use AI to write this report.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nSimply run the attached MRP. If you change `@export var use_texture_padding := true` so that it's `false`, the issue won't repro anymore.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[DoubleFreeRepro.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/31927966/DoubleFreeRepro.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123289/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123289/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}